{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-yekutieli-triple","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:yekutieli-triple","kind":"definition","title":"Lifting triple mapping","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-descent"],"tags":["yekutieli","triple","gerbe","transition-function"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.CosimplicialCrossedGroupoid.YekutieliTriple","text":"yekutieli-triple.md","leanSource":"yekutieli-triple.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:yekutieli-triple\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe with recursive brane tower <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{A_n\\}_{n \\geq 0}</code> (<a href=\"#def:recursive-brane-tower\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation\">recursive brane tower</a>) and substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{U_i\\}</code> be a covering of the underlying site <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}</code> trivialising every level of the tower. The <strong>Yekutieli lifting triple</strong> at level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> over an intersection <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U_i \\cap U_j</code> is the datum <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(x_{ij}^{(n)}, g_{ij}^{(n)}, a_{ij}^{(n)})</code>, where:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Objects.</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x_i^{(n)} \\in \\mathrm{Ob}(\\mathfrak{G}_n|_{U_i})</code> are local trivialisations of the Frobenius--Hopf object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_n</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>-morphisms.</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g_{ij}^{(n)} \\colon x_i^{(n)} \\to x_j^{(n)}</code> are the transition automorphisms in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Aut}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A_n|_{U_i \\cap U_j})</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code>-morphisms.</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a_{ij}^{(n)} \\colon g_{ij}^{(n)} \\Rightarrow g_{ij}^{(n+1)}</code> are the deformation parameters living in the band <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{B}</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-triple.md","heading":"Definition","number":"6.10.1","page":"b/def-yekutieli-triple","qa":{"counts":{"pass":83,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":8,"unknown":0,"stale":64},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.CosimplicialCrossedGroupoid.YekutieliTriple","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-triple.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
